---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout title="Download" description="Install Cove with Docker, native downloads, or from source.">
  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow-small">Install</p>
      <h1 class="page-heading">Download Cove</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">Cove is free, open source forever, and built to run on hardware you control. Start with Docker, use a native build, or migrate your existing Stash library forward.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner download-grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Docker all-in-one</h3>
        <p>Recommended for most server installs. Starts Cove, PostgreSQL, and FFmpeg together so you can open the web UI and finish setup.</p>
        <div class="code-block"><pre><code>cd docker&#10;docker compose -f docker-compose.allinone.yml up -d</code></pre></div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Native builds</h3>
        <p>Download a platform release when you want a single app-style install. Cove bundles the frontend and backend, auto-manages PostgreSQL and FFmpeg, and applies database migrations on startup.</p>
        <ul class="link-list">
          <li><strong>Windows, macOS, Linux:</strong> platform builds from GitHub Releases.</li>
          <li><strong>Source builds:</strong> clone the repository when you want to inspect or modify Cove.</li>
          <li><strong>Internet exposure:</strong> use your own reverse proxy and security layer.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner setup-grid">
      <article class="setup-card step-card"><h3>Download and install</h3><p>Start with Docker or a native build, open Cove, and follow the simple installation wizard.</p></article>
      <article class="setup-card step-card"><h3>Add media</h3><p>Point Cove at a folder, import from Stash, or use downloader workflows as your collection grows.</p></article>
      <article class="setup-card step-card"><h3>Scan and review</h3><p>Cove indexes files, generates media, finds metadata, and lets you review changes instead of blindly accepting everything.</p></article>
      <article class="setup-card step-card"><h3>Make it yours</h3><p>Choose a theme, save filters, set permissions, enable extensions, and build the workflow that fits your collection.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner info-grid">
      <article class="info-card"><h3>No account required</h3><p>Cove runs on your machine or server. Your files, generated previews, users, and metadata stay where you put them.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Bring Stash with you</h3><p>If you're moving from Stash, Cove can import your library and keep going with improved performace, broader media support, real users and groups, and a deeper extension system.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Open source</h3><p>The code is available for inspection, contribution, and self-hosted use.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
